    "text": "By Donna Iadipaolo ,\n1 days ago For nearly 11 months, the lights were off at Juicy Kitchen. The popular Ann Arbor café, known for its fresh, locally sourced breakfasts, smoothies, and prepared foods, sat silent after a freezer fire forced it to close. What began as what many hoped would be a straightforward restoration quickly evolved into an extensive renovation filled with construction delays, insurance hurdles and unexpected code requirements. Read full article",
